  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Schoenberg proved that for every $c\\in [0,1]$ the density of $ \\{ n\\in \\mathbb{N} : \\phi(n)<cn\\} $ exists. Let this density be denoted by $f(c)$. Is it true that there are no $x$ such that $f'(x)$ exists and is positive?",
